Method (Heuer): 
1. Generate {{ min_hypotheses }}-{{ max_hypotheses }} mutually exclusive, plausible hypotheses that explain the activity, always including a benign/organic explanation and a null hypothesis where relevant.
2. For each evidence item, judge whether it is Consistent (C), Inconsistent (I), or Not applicable/Neutral (N) with each hypothesis. Focus on diagnostic evidence -- items that discriminate between hypotheses.
3. Rank hypotheses by the LEAST inconsistent evidence (not by most consistent).
4. Assign each hypothesis a likelihood using WEP ({{ wep_terms | join(", ") }}) and a confidence level.
5. Identify the evidence that, if it changed, would most alter the ranking (linchpin evidence) and what collection would test each hypothesis.

